+# tasks-api
+
+A multi-tenant task tracking API built with [Bun](https://bun.sh),
+[Elysia](https://elysiajs.com) and [Drizzle ORM](https://orm.drizzle.team) on
+SQLite (libSQL). Organizations own users, projects and tasks; every
+authenticated request is scoped to the caller's organization.
+
+## Running locally
+
+Requires Bun 1.4.3 (pinned in `package.json` under `packageManager`).
+
+```sh
+# 1. Install dependencies
+bun install
+
+# 2. Configure the environment (Bun loads .env automatically)
+cp .env.example .env
+
+# 3. Create the database and apply migrations
+mkdir -p data          # libSQL will not create the parent directory
+bun run db:migrate
+
+# 4. Load demo data (see "Seed data" below)
+bun run db:seed
+
+# 5. Start the dev server with file watching
+bun run dev
+```
+
+The API listens on `http://localhost:4000` by default. Check it with:
+
+```sh
+curl http://localhost:4000/api/health
+# {"status":"ok"}
+```
+
+The server also applies pending migrations on startup, so step 3 is mainly
+needed before seeding.
+
+The seed script inserts fixed IDs and fails if run against a database that is
+already seeded. To start over, delete the database file and repeat steps 3–4:
+
+```sh
+rm data/dev.db && bun run db:migrate && bun run db:seed
+```
+
+### Other scripts
+
+| Script                 | Purpose                                                |
+| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `bun run start`        | Start the server without file watching                 |
+| `bun run build`        | Bundle `src/index.ts` into `dist/`                     |
+| `bun run test`         | Run the Vitest suite                                   |
+| `bun run typecheck`    | Type-check with `tsc --noEmit`                         |
+| `bun run lint`         | Run ESLint                                             |
+| `bun run format:check` | Check formatting with Prettier (`format:fix` to write) |
+| `bun run db:generate`  | Generate a new migration from `src/db/schema.ts`       |
+
+Migrations live in `drizzle/`.
+
+## Environment variables
+
+| Variable          | Default            | Description                                                                                                               |
+| ----------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `PORT`            | `4000`             | HTTP port for the server.                                                                                                 |
+| `DATABASE_URL`    | `file:data/dev.db` | libSQL connection URL. Used by the server, the migrate/seed scripts and `drizzle-kit`.                                    |
+| `WEBHOOK_SECRET`  | _(none)_           | Shared secret expected in the `x-webhook-secret` header of billing webhooks. If unset, every webhook request is rejected. |
+| `TOKEN_TTL_HOURS` | `24`               | Lifetime of API tokens issued by `POST /api/auth/token`.                                                                  |
+| `LOG_LEVEL`       | `info`             | One of `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error`, `silent`. Logs are JSON lines on stdout/stderr.                                  |
+
+Tests set `LOG_LEVEL=silent`, `WEBHOOK_SECRET=test-webhook-secret` and
+`TOKEN_TTL_HOURS=24` unless they are already defined (`src/test/setup.ts`).
+
+## Seed data
+
+`bun run db:seed` creates two organizations. All users share the password
+`password123`, and each has a long-lived bearer token for local use.
+
+| User               | Organization          | Role   | Token                    |
+| ------------------ | --------------------- | ------ | ------------------------ |
+| `ada@acme.test`    | Acme (`org_acme`)     | admin  | `dev-acme-admin-token`   |
+| `bob@acme.test`    | Acme (`org_acme`)     | member | `dev-acme-member-token`  |
+| `gina@globex.test` | Globex (`org_globex`) | admin  | `dev-globex-admin-token` |
+
+Acme has the projects `prj_web`, `prj_app` and `prj_billing`; Globex has
+`prj_infra`. Tasks `tsk_1` to `tsk_6` are spread across them.
+
+These tokens are for development only. Never seed them into a production
+database.
+
+## Authentication
+
+Routes marked **auth** need an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header. Get a
+token from `POST /api/auth/token`, or use a seed token:
+
+```sh
+curl -H "Authorization: Bearer dev-acme-admin-token" http://localhost:4000/api/me
+```
+
+A missing header returns `401` with
+`{"code":"unauthenticated","message":"missing bearer token"}`. An unknown or
+expired token returns `401` with the plain-text body `Unauthorized`.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+All paths are prefixed with `/api`. Request bodies are JSON. Requests that
+fail schema validation return `422` with Elysia's validation error body.
+Unknown routes return `404`.
+
+| Method   | Path                      | Auth           | Description                         |
+| -------- | ------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------- |
+| `GET`    | `/api/health`             | none           | Liveness check                      |
+| `POST`   | `/api/auth/token`         | none           | Exchange email/password for a token |
+| `GET`    | `/api/me`                 | auth           | Current user                        |
+| `GET`    | `/api/projects`           | auth           | List the organization's projects    |
+| `POST`   | `/api/projects`           | auth           | Create a project                    |
+| `GET`    | `/api/projects/:id`       | auth           | Get a project                       |
+| `GET`    | `/api/projects/:id/tasks` | auth           | List a project's tasks              |
+| `POST`   | `/api/projects/:id/tasks` | auth           | Create a task in a project          |
+| `GET`    | `/api/tasks/:id`          | auth           | Get a task                          |
+| `PATCH`  | `/api/tasks/:id`          | auth           | Update a task                       |
+| `DELETE` | `/api/tasks/:id`          | auth (admin)   | Delete a task                       |
+| `POST`   | `/api/webhooks/billing`   | webhook secret | Billing provider webhook            |
+
+### `GET /api/health`
+
+Returns `{"status":"ok"}`.
+
+### `POST /api/auth/token`
+
+```json
+{ "email": "ada@acme.test", "password": "password123" }
+```
+
+The email is matched case-insensitively. Returns
+`{"token": "...", "expiresAt": "<ISO timestamp>"}`. The token expires after
+`TOKEN_TTL_HOURS`. Wrong credentials return `401`
+`{"error":"invalid email or password"}`.
+
+### `GET /api/me`
+
+Returns `id`, `orgId`, `role` (`admin` or `member`), `email` and `name` for the
+token's user.
+
+### `GET /api/projects`
+
+Lists the caller's organization's projects, sorted by name. Each item has a
+task count per status:
+
+```json
+{
+  "items": [
+    {
+      "id": "prj_web",
+      "name": "Website relaunch",
+      "description": "New marketing site",
+      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T09:00:00.000Z",
+      "taskCounts": { "todo": 1, "in_progress": 1, "done": 1 }
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### `POST /api/projects`
+
+| Field         | Type   | Rules                  |
+| ------------- | ------ | ---------------------- |
+| `name`        | string | required, 1–100 chars  |
+| `description` | string | optional, ≤ 2000 chars |
+
+Returns `201` with the stored project row (`id`, `orgId`, `name`,
+`description`, `createdAt`).
+
+### `GET /api/projects/:id`
+
+Returns the project row. Returns `404` (plain text `Project not found`) if the
+project doesn't exist or belongs to another organization.
+
+### `GET /api/projects/:id/tasks`
+
+Returns `{"items": [Task, ...]}`, sorted by creation time. Same `404` rule as
+above.
+
+A **Task** looks like this:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "tsk_3",
+  "projectId": "prj_web",
+  "title": "Fix broken signup link",
+  "description": null,
+  "status": "todo",
+  "isUrgent": true,
+  "assigneeId": "usr_ada",
+  "dueDate": null,
+  "createdAt": "2026-10-01T09:03:00.000Z",
+  "updatedAt": "2026-10-01T09:03:00.000Z"
+}
+```
+
+`status` is one of `todo`, `in_progress` or `done`. `dueDate` is a
+`YYYY-MM-DD` string.
+
+### `POST /api/projects/:id/tasks`
+
+| Field         | Type    | Rules                                |
+| ------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |
+| `title`       | string  | required, 1–200 chars                |
+| `description` | string  | optional, ≤ 5000 chars               |
+| `isUrgent`    | boolean | optional, defaults to `false`        |
+| `assigneeId`  | string  | optional, must be a user in your org |
+| `dueDate`     | string  | optional, `YYYY-MM-DD`               |
+
+New tasks start as `todo`. Returns `201` with the Task. If `assigneeId` is not
+a member of the caller's organization the response is `400`. When a task is
+created with an assignee, that user gets an assignment email. Locally the
+mailer only logs a `mail.sent` line.
+
+### `GET /api/tasks/:id`
+
+Returns the Task, or `404` `{"error":"task not found"}`.
+
+### `PATCH /api/tasks/:id`
+
+Every field is optional. Only the fields you send are changed.
+
+| Field         | Type           | Rules                                        |
+| ------------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
+| `title`       | string         | ≤ 200 chars; trimmed, must not be blank      |
+| `description` | string \| null | ≤ 5000 chars                                 |
+| `status`      | enum           | `todo`, `in_progress` or `done`; see below   |
+| `isUrgent`    | boolean        |                                              |
+| `assigneeId`  | string \| null | must be a user in your org; `null` unassigns |
+| `dueDate`     | string \| null | `YYYY-MM-DD`; `null` clears                  |
+
+Allowed status transitions:
+
+| From          | To                   |
+| ------------- | -------------------- |
+| `todo`        | `in_progress`        |
+| `in_progress` | `todo`, `done`       |
+| `done`        | `todo` (admins only) |
+
+Errors:
+
+- `404` the task doesn't exist in the caller's organization.
+- `400` blank title, or an assignee outside the organization.
+- `403` a non-admin tries to reopen a `done` task.
+- `409` the status transition isn't allowed; the task would be marked `done`
+  with no assignee; or a due date is set on a `done` task.
+
+Returns the updated Task. When the assignee changes to a new user, that user
+gets an assignment email.
+
+### `DELETE /api/tasks/:id`
+
+Admins only. Non-admins get `403` (plain text `Forbidden`). Returns `204` on
+success, or `404` `{"error":"task not found"}` if the task doesn't exist in
+the caller's organization.
+
+### `POST /api/webhooks/billing`
+
+Called by the billing provider. Doesn't use a bearer token: the
+`x-webhook-secret` header must equal `WEBHOOK_SECRET`, otherwise the response
+is `401` (plain text `invalid webhook secret`).
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "evt_123",
+  "type": "payment.succeeded",
+  "data": { "orgId": "org_acme", "credits": 50 }
+}
+```
+
+For `payment.succeeded`, `data.credits` (a non-negative integer, default `0`)
+is added to the organization's credit balance. Other event types are accepted
+and ignored. Always returns `{"received":true}` once authenticated and valid.
+
+```sh
+curl -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/webhooks/billing \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -H "x-webhook-secret: change-me" \
+  -d '{"id":"evt_123","type":"payment.succeeded","data":{"orgId":"org_acme","credits":50}}'
+```
